`fix-it` task 1 is done. `pnpm test` (30 files, 403 tests), `pnpm typecheck` and `pnpm secret-scan` all pass. I did not commit anything or touch `.kiro/agents`.

- **Redaction:** `lib/fix/redact.ts` has `redactToken` and `safeMessage` (R1.10, R1.11).
- **Planning:** `lib/fix/plan.ts` has the zod schemas, `parseRepoSlug`, `planFix`, `whyOf`, `prBody`, `commitMessage`, `branchName` and `prTitle` (R1.1–R1.9).
- **Slug rule:** `lib/github/repo.ts` now exports `isRepoName`, so the repo-name rule has one source.
- **Tests:** `tests/fix-redact.test.ts` and `tests/fix-plan.test.ts` were written before the code. They use fast-check for token removal, idempotence, link-span-only changes with BOM/CRLF/no-final-newline, path and slug rules, and the 60,000-character PR body cap.

**Bug found and fixed:** `extractMarkdownLinks` returned spans one character too early on any file that starts with a byte-order mark, because the Markdown parser drops the BOM before counting offsets. Patching such a file would have corrupted it. I fixed it in `lib/extract/markdown.ts` and added a regression test in `tests/markdown.test.ts`.

**Bookkeeping:** Task 1 is ticked in `.kiro/specs/fix-it/tasks.md`. `KIRO_USAGE.md` has a dated 26 Nov 2026 line saying it was built in Kiro CLI by the `gravedigger` agent via `scripts/kiro/run-task.sh fix-it 1`.

**Placement choices:**
- `branchName(now, random)` takes a `random: () => number` returning values in [0, 1). The task 2 writer will pass a crypto-backed one.
- `planFix` returns `title` and `body` as well as `files` and `links`. Each file also carries its commit `message`.
- In the PR table, `|` inside the old-URL code span is escaped as well. GitHub otherwise splits the cell there.
